{
  "requirement": "`record.is_current(graph, version)` returns `Ok(false)` immediately if the criterion version is incompatible. For a compatible version, it checks each saved dependency against the graph, stopping at the first changed fingerprint or domain error. An empty dependency list passes.\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl<N, L> Record<N, L> {\n    pub fn is_current<D>(\n        &self,\n        graph: &D,\n        version: &CriterionVersion,\n    ) -> Result<bool, D::Error>\n    where\n        D: Domain<NodeId = N, EdgeLabel = L>;\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests cover every obligation in `requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.record.is_current`.\n\n**Incompatible version returns `Ok(false)` immediately.** `record_freshness_short_circuits_before_later_graph_reads` in `validation_tests.rs` saves version v1 and checks against v2. It asserts `Ok(false)`. It also asserts that the graph's `reads` list is empty, so no dependency was read (\"immediately\"). What counts as a compatible version is the job of the `checking_records.version_match` requirement, not this subject.\n\n**Empty dependency list passes.** The same test asserts `Ok(true)` for a record with no dependencies and a compatible version.\n\n**Domain error stops the check.** In the same test, the record has two dependencies, node 1 and node 2. Node 1 is missing, so the check returns `Err(\"missing\")`. The test asserts that `reads == [1]`, so the check stopped at the first error and never read node 2.\n\n**Changed fingerprint stops the check.** After node 1's content changes, the same test asserts `Ok(false)` and `reads == [1]`. So it stops at the first changed fingerprint and does not read node 2.\n\n**Checks each dependency, so a later change is not hidden.** `a_matching_dependency_does_not_hide_a_later_changed_dependency` first asserts the record is current while both dependencies match. It then changes only the later dependency, and the first one stays unchanged. The test asserts that this gives `Ok(false)`. It runs for both a `Dependency::Node` and a `Dependency::OutgoingEdges` later dependency, so each dependency kind is checked.\n\n`public_exports_match_the_appendix` only checks the public API inventory. It adds nothing for this requirement, and nothing else is needed from it.\n\nI found no plausible behavior that violates the requirement and that these tests would accept.",
  "references": "0985e2391bbea0b5f1c8774e47e2da5e8fb3715db44dae99d5dc8dc59248c292",
